  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 760324,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 1991 Du Ma Racing: A Galloping Good Time (or Gamble!)\n\nStep into the world of 1991 Du Ma Racing, an unlicensed horse racing game for the Nintendo Entertainment System developed by Idea-Tek and published by Super Mega. Originally released in Taiwan, this title offers a unique blend of competitive racing and strategic betting.\n\nThe game features two distinct modes to satisfy different playstyles. In *Race Mode*, two players can test their skills against each other. Success hinges on precise timing – pressing buttons at the perfect moment to build up your horse's power and unleash it for a speed boost. Accuracy and speed are key to victory!\n\nFor those who prefer a more relaxed approach, *Gamble Mode* allows 1 to 6 players to wager on five horses in simulated races. With starting credits of 500, players strategically place their bets and watch as AI-controlled horses compete. The ultimate goal? Accumulate more wealth than your fellow gamblers. 1991 Du Ma Racing provides a simple yet engaging experience for NES enthusiasts seeking a fresh, albeit unusual, racing adventure."
    },
